"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a lead from Sarah Tan in the Analytics Department. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th. Initially, the budget was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and the integration of real-time analytics. Additional budgets were approved for a compliance plan ($55,000) and training programs ($15,000). The project involves gathering ideas by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a prototype for secure file sharing, which was achieved ahead of schedule. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year. A celebration for the testing milestone is planned for October 10th."
